Back Market is a French online marketplace dedicated exclusively to refurbished electronics, connecting vetted refurbishment professionals with consumers seeking quality-assured renewed devices. The platform has sold over 30 million refurbished products globally, saving an estimated 1.6 million tonnes of carbon emissions. A critical innovation is Back Market's quality grading system: every seller is vetted before being allowed on the platform and continuously monitored through test orders, ensuring consistent product quality across hundreds of independent refurbishers. Products are graded by cosmetic condition (Fair, Good, Excellent, Premium), with clear descriptions and standardised warranties of at least 12 months. This assessability infrastructure — transparent grading, consistent quality standards, and warranty backing — has been instrumental in building consumer trust in refurbished products. The platform operates in 13 countries and hosts over 1,000 sellers, demonstrating that a marketplace model built around rigorous assessment and quality assurance can scale refurbishment from a niche to a mainstream consumer choice.